Z||000005||FieroSTETZ||04-29-2001||11:18 AM||||condensation, i had just finished washing it and sprayed the back of the car - you cant hear it but it was gurgling and stuff for a few minutes - that engine (before it's demise) was cammed, had a really cool induction system, the prior owner (found through DMV) said that the engine had been built up to 10.5:1 compression, and had been his baby - explains why i barely passed smog everytime - if someone in the room had flatulated, i woulda failed smog - the new engine was built to my specs to be "as light as is reasonable possible" so it has aluminum heads and a lot of lightweight parts, but i also specified durability was key. i think i have a new favorite person (the guy that buiilt it!)||||reg||1
